  "narrative": "No new validation results or response deadlines arrived this cycle; the validation quota is exhausted, so conclusions must rest on existing discovery and previously received validation evidence. The most important update is H196, the reversed interaction of feature_063 with feature_018. Its signed estimate is +0.429 with 95% bounds +0.247 to +0.611. This is well above the 0.15 threshold and excludes the threshold comfortably, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association. Interpreted relative to the accepted negative feature_063 contrasts, the positive interaction means that the feature_063 negative association is much stronger in the feature_018<=0 complement than in the feature_018>=0 subgroup; high feature_018 attenuates feature_063's association with lower outcome_001. This reconciles H188 and H189: the high-feature_038, feature_027/feature_037-absent feature_063 signal is robust among low feature_018 participants (H189), while the high feature_018 stratum is imprecise and weaker (H188). I closed H175, H184, H186, and H189 as mature accepted context claims because their central conclusions are no longer open; H188 and H197 remain the key unresolved extensions.\n\nSupported dataset-specific findings are now coherent. feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are strong positive associations with outcome_001, with large effects that persist in many strata and are supported by validation for feature_002 overall and in feature_010-negative participants. feature_027=1 and feature_037=1 are strong negative associations with outcome_001; these are replicated in validation and remain large when evaluated apart from the other major tags. feature_063 is not a uniform tag. It shows strong negative associations in contexts where feature_038 is high and the major negative tags feature_027 and feature_037 are absent (H175, H184, H176, H154/H155), especially when positive tags feature_010 and feature_002 are absent (H186). Its association is further concentrated among low feature_018 participants (H189, H196), but attenuation by high feature_018 does not by itself prove independence; it is an association measured through the supplied binary splits.\n\nImportant negative or unsupported findings: the three constructed binary research markers feature_007, feature_058, and feature_015 are not associated with scientifically meaningful outcome_001 differences; H5 was validated and remains rejected. Most categorical predictors tested were null or imprecise. feature_063 is not supported as a negative association in low-feature_038 core-negative territory (H168, H185, H190) and is not robust in small positive-tag-absent contexts such as H162, H170, H179, or H187; those remain unresolved rather than evidence of zero. H79 rejects a positive marginal feature_063 effect. H182 rejects the opposite feature_018 interaction direction, and H194 rejects the conditional feature_017 negative screen. H191 is too imprecise to support attenuation or synergy with feature_037. Conditional low-prevalence screens H192 and H193 remain underpowered positive suggestions rather than supported findings. Age/feature_019 contrasts remain unresolved: H195 is unusable due to insufficient cells, and earlier age tests are either rejected or too imprecise.\n\nUnresolved uncertainty includes: the marginal overall feature_063 negative association H80, which is suggestive and validated but has intervals that do not cleanly establish population magnitude above the 0.15 threshold; the high-feature_018 main contrast within the high-feature_038 core-negative context (H188); whether the feature_018 attenuation survives after removing positive tags (newly proposed direct interaction proposal); the role of feature_036 and other assay interactions; small feature_063-positive contexts; conditional feature_022 and feature_016 screens; and feature_019 age contrasts. The most informative next analyses are therefore the newly proposed cleaner-context feature_063 tests: (1) high feature_038, low feature_018, all major positive and negative tags absent; (2) low feature_038, all major positive and negative tags absent; (3) low feature_038, core-negative territory, low feature_018; (4) high feature_038, high feature_018, all major positive and negative tags absent; and (5) the direct feature_063-by-feature_018 interaction in the same high-feature_038, tag-absent setting. These target the remaining boundary between a robust context-specific negative association and an overlocalized/small-cell pattern. All conclusions are associations in the supplied dataset only; they do not establish causality, mechanism, biological meaning, clinical relevance, or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 15 synthesis: validation quota exhausted; no new validation to assess. Accepted H196 (feature_018 attenuation of feature_063 negative association) from R172. Closed mature accepted feature_063 context claims H175, H184, H186, H189. Current model: feature_010/feature_002 strong positive tags; feature_027/feature_037 strong negative tags; feature_063 is context-dependent negative, strongest high feature_038 when feature_027/feature_037 are absent, and stronger among feature_018<=0 than feature_018>=0. Low feature_038 and small positive-tag feature_063 contexts are unsupported or imprecise. H80 marginal overall feature_063 remains unresolved despite suggestive replication because intervals do not cleanly clear 0.15. Next priority: clean-context feature_063 tests just proposed, especially the direct high-feature_038/tag-absent feature_018 interaction and main effects split by feature_018. Also preserve unresolved low-prevalence screens (feature_022, feature_016) and age feature_019 as secondary. Treat insufficient-cell results as unusable. No causal, mechanistic, biological, clinical, or generalizable claims."
